    // implementation, MIT: on an M4 Pro a mismatched cube reads face 0 in every direction through a cube array argument and layer 0 at every index through a 2D array argument). A cube read
    // as 2D is face 0, as a non-array sample of a 2D array is layer 0; a cube read as a cube array is a one-cube cube array view, as Ryujinx does (Texture.GetTargetTexture: CubemapArray view
    // of depth 6; Splatoon 3 10-26 binds an NVN cube to a slot its shader declares a cube array). A Metal cube's arrayLength is 1 and a cube array's counts cubes
    NSUInteger layers = have == MTLTextureType2D ? 1 : have == MTLTextureType2DArray ? t.arrayLength : have == MTLTextureTypeCube || have == MTLTextureTypeCubeArray ? t.arrayLength * 6 : 0;
