    // a defined read, instead of a type mismatch whose reads are undefined. The same for a 2D array of fewer than 6 layers, which is how the host holds some 2D textures (Mario Kart 8 Deluxe binds
    // an NVN 2D texture, format 0x44, at slot 10 of two pixel shaders that declare a cube there, as a race loads). Ryujinx does the same without a report: a 2D texture has no cube target
    // (Texture.GetTargetTexture → IsSameDimensionsTarget false → null), so the slot reads as unbound. A legal binding the game makes, logged once, not reported as red
    if (!ns && (want == MTLTextureTypeCube || want == MTLTextureTypeCubeArray) && (have == MTLTextureType2D || (have == MTLTextureType2DArray && t.arrayLength < 6))) {
